    - target: {fileID: 2011556165753655389, guid: 10e6230c3c0c327468cddde56523fdbe, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Text
      value: "That's correct!\n\nThe rune stones are A, B, and C. Since order matters,
        each different arrangement of two stones in the slots forms a new result.
        This is called a permutation.\n\nLet\u2019s list them:\n\nAB, AC, BA, BC,
        CA, CB\n\nThere are 6 total arrangements.\n\nWe can calculate this using
        permutation notation:\n\nP(3,2) = \\frac{3!}{(3\u22122)!} = \\frac{3 x 2
        x 1}{1} = 6\n\nThe three rune stones have 6 permutations when selecting two
        at a time.\u201D"
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
